  "question": "Do the combined immutable R24D10 and R24D14 finite development records satisfy every mechanism-coverage prerequisite previously declared by R24D3 and made explicit by R24D11, such that the exact Godot/Jolt active-step-snapshot v2 runtime profile may be promoted as the measured source for the two missing exact-s169 recovery channels?",
  "answer": "Yes, within the exact runtime-profile scope only. R24D10 already retained the signed drive, positive-work, source-cap, disabled-zero, limit-separation, invalid-timing/RID-refusal, and current-versus-stale mechanism families. R24D11 refused promotion solely because the signed braking cells lacked opposing impulse and absorbed work. R24D14, on the identical source patch and retained binary pair, validly observed both signed enabled braking witnesses and both paired disabled exact-zero controls under the predeclared R24D11 witness rule. The exact instrumented profile is therefore promoted as an eligible measured source for applied-actuation receipts and the dependent energy-balance ledger. This decision does not promote stock Godot, accept numerical accuracy, implement the live adapter mapping, complete the three-engine capability conjunction, or open recovery or prone-to-standing.",
