    "braking_witness_rule": "Both signed motor-enabled braking cells must retain a nonzero motor impulse opposing the declared nonzero initial canonical rate, strictly positive absorbed motor work, and strictly negative net motor work; both paired disabled cells must retain exact-zero motor impulse and all three motor-work channels.",
    "decision_rule": "Promote only the exact instrumented runtime profile when the immutable R24D10 record satisfies the seven previously observed mechanism families, the immutable R24D14 record satisfies the predeclared missing signed-braking witness rule in both directions with paired disabled controls, and the runtime source, patch, console binary, and engine binary identities match exactly.",
    "adequacy_argument": "The R24D3 mechanism list was fixed before either accepted physical result, and R24D11 made the sole missing braking witness explicit before R24D14. R24D10 and R24D14 execute the same source patch and exact retained binary pair. Their complete finite records are therefore adequate to decide whether this exact instrumented profile exposes every required measurement mechanism needed to author a profile-scoped recovery capability mapping. They are not a repeated or held-out cohort, do not establish numerical accuracy, and do not justify stock-Godot, arbitrary-hinge, morphology, recovery-performance, prone-to-standing, robustness, cross-engine-equivalence, superiority, non-inferiority, physical-acceptance, release, or population claims."
